From 3c3a471b76230d876be8355ae9cc4eb7febc1044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:41:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bump VERSION to match the released 0.5.1 PyPI sdist

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [upstream never commits its release version bumps back to git]

master's setup.py has been stuck at VERSION = (0, 4, 0) since 954c61f3
(2024-05-02), even though PyPI has since shipped 0.5.0 and then 0.5.1
sdists. Diffing the 0.5.1 sdist against this commit's tree shows
src/farmhash.{cc,h}, src/python-farmhash.{cc,h}, LICENSE, MANIFEST.in
and README.md are all byte-identical: the maintainer bumps the VERSION
tuple locally before running the release build and never pushes that
one-line change back to git. Apply the same bump here so the wheel we
publish reports the version pip already resolves from PyPI.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index c7c4c5a..a1c2c18 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 
 from setuptools import setup, find_packages, Extension
 
-VERSION = (0, 4, 0)
+VERSION = (0, 5, 1)
 
 setup(
     name='pyfarmhash',
-- 
2.50.1 (Apple Git-155)

